#: ../../chapter05.rst:3
msgid "Management Console"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:5
msgid ""
"If you are logged in as the Tenant administrator, access the Management "
"Console by clicking the gear icon on the top right of the **\"File "
"Browser\"** view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:7
msgid ""
"The Tenant Administrator will see the files and folders view by default "
"upon initial login."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:13
msgid ""
"If you are the cluster administrator, you may not see the \"Management "
"Console\" icon. Instead, you can manage the default tenant from the "
"Cluster Manager -> Tenant Manager and click through to manage the default"
" tenant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:17
msgid "Here is the Tenant Management Console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:21
msgid ""
"Please reference the `CentreStack Admin Guide`_ for complete details "
"about Tenant administration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:23
msgid "Here are a few points that are more important during the deployment phase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:26
msgid "Add Tenant"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:28
msgid ""
"You can add a tenant by clicking the 'New Tenant' Button in the Tenant "
"Manager"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:34
msgid "Team Folders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:36
msgid ""
"Team Folders are created by the tenant admin. The users that can be "
"assigned to the team folders are the team users within the tenant. Each "
"team user can be assigned read or write permissions to the team folder. "
"For the team users that are not assigned with a specific team folder, the"
" team folder will not show up. Team folders users can also be assigned "
"the \"Owner\" permission. The owner permission allows the \"owner\" to "
"maintain and manage the team folder permissions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:42
msgid ""
"You can navigate to the Team Folders by clicking on the \"Team Folders\" "
"tab from the left side menu of Tenant Manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:44
msgid "Here is the Team Folders page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:50
msgid "User Manager"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:52
msgid ""
"In the user manager, you can create users, import users from Active "
"Directory over LDAP or import users from Active Directory via Server "
"Agent. Click on the \"Users\" tab from the left side menu of Tenant "
"Manager. Then click on \"Create or Migrate Users\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:58
msgid "This should take you to a menu of options to add a new user to the tenant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:64
msgid "Delegate Administration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:66
msgid ""
"You can add full delegated admin to the list of \"Cloud Administrators\"."
" Once you reach the tenant dashboard, click \"Settings\" from left side "
"menu, and then go to the \"User Account & Security\". In \"User Account &"
" Security\", Click on \"Tenant Administrators\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:72
msgid ""
"At the bottom of the Tenant Administrators page, you can designate the "
"delegated admin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:77
msgid "Active Directory Integration (Optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:79
msgid ""
"It is optional to setup the Active Directory Integration. You can get to "
"the integration page from the Management Console -> Settings -> Active "
"Directory Settings. The active directory setting here refers to local "
"Active Directory with LDAP integration. For remote Active Directory, "
"server agent can be used to connect remote file server folders and remote"
" Active Directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:84
msgid ""
"Once you reach the tenant dashboard, click \"Settings\" from left side "
"menu, and then go to the \"Active Directory\" option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:88
msgid ""
"This will take you to the Active Directory Page. After you turn on the "
"switch and enable Active Directory Integration, you can fill in your "
"information for Active Directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:94
msgid ""
"If this specific tenant's Active Directory is at a remote location, "
"please use the CentreStack Server Agent to connect the Active Directory "
"(No need to use LDAP over Internet WAN connection)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:100
msgid "Branding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:102
msgid ""
"You can brand the web portal, Windows and Mac clients, iOS and Android "
"Applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:104
msgid ""
"The self-service branding starts with the \"Cluster Manager\". In order "
"to start the branding, you will login to the web portal as the Cluster "
"Administrator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:107
msgid ""
"After you login to the web portal, click to the \"Cluster Branding\" "
"Pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter05.rst:111
msgid ""
"Please reference the \"Cluster Branding\" section in the `Admin Guide`_ "
"for the self-hosted CentreStack server."
msgstr ""

